{
  "id": "per-base-cancel-overrun",
  "measured": "2026-09-02",
  "published": false,
  "source": {
    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "pnpm --filter @jbrowse/web build, then in products/jbrowse-web: node browser-tests/probe-per-base-refetch.ts --fixture=trio, and node browser-tests/probe-per-base-refetch.ts --fixture=fam --data=~/data/fam — the cancelMidFetch rows",
    "notes": "Same harness and fixtures as per-base-zoom-refetch. One zoom-in click issues the octave refetch; 80ms after that call is in flight, view.setDisplayedRegions replaces the region set, which is the DisplayedRegionsChange cancel (clearAllRpcData → cancelFetch → stopStopToken). \"stopped\" is when the token was revoked, \"settled\" when the RPC promise resolved, both from the call being issued. Every row resolved with data rather than an AbortError; the main thread discarded it through ctx.isStale()."
  },
  "columns": [
    {
      "key": "case",
      "label": "case"
    },
    {
      "key": "stoppedMs",
      "label": "token stopped at",
      "format": "ms",
      "align": "right"
    },
    {
      "key": "settledMs",
      "label": "RPC settled at",
      "format": "ms",
      "align": "right"
    },
    {
      "key": "pastStopMs",
      "label": "ran past the stop",
      "format": "ms",
      "align": "right"
    },
    {
      "key": "statusAfterStop",
      "label": "status messages after the stop",
      "format": "int",
      "align": "right"
    },
    {
      "key": "outcome",
      "label": "outcome"
    }
  ],
  "rows": [
